"Hey!" calls Sarah, your colleague, "I see you've already started with Git. Next you should learn how to stage changes."

She explains: "When you modify files, you need to explicitly tell Git which changes should be included in the next commit. 
This is called 'staging' and works with git add."
Real-World Context
The staging concept is a powerful feature of Git. It allows you to commit only selected changes while others can remain in progress.



git add . ( add all files at once)

