Remove files: git rm <file> (<> not necessary)
The 3 Steps to Sync with GitHub

*****Using git rm is just the first part of a three-step chain reaction:

git rm filename.txt
This deletes the file from your local folder and automatically stages the deletion. It tells Git, "Hey, I want to get rid of this file." (At this point, GitHub still has the file).

git commit -m "Remove unnecessary files"
This locks the deletion into your local repository's history. (GitHub still has the file).

git push
This uploads your new history to GitHub. Now, GitHub updates, and the file disappears from your online repository.


